      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I factor in the cost of water in liquid formulations?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Water may seem free, but industrial-grade DI (Deionized) or RO (Reverse Osmosis) water has filtration and pumping costs. Technically, water should be costed based on the energy and maintenance required for the purification system used in your facility."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the typical profit margin in specialty chemical formulations?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Margins vary widely, but specialty chemicals generally command gross margins of 40% to 150%, depending on the technical difficulty and the niche solved. Commodities (like bleach or basic solvents) operate on much lower margins, often below 15-20%."
      }
    },
